## 🎬 30-minute live demo runbook

Assuming Airflow is already installed (step 1 above done ahead of time):

| Time | What you do | What it shows |
|---|---|---|
| 0–5 min | `source scripts/local_dev_env.sh && airflow standalone` in one terminal | Airflow booting on real Postgres, LocalExecutor |
| 5–8 min | Log in, Admin > Connections > add `analytics_db` | Zero-code data connection setup |
| 8–10 min | Admin > Variables > add the two tuning knobs | Runtime config with no redeploy |
| 10–12 min | Unpause `earthquake_medallion_pipeline`, hit Trigger | Kicking off a real pipeline run |
| 12–18 min | Grid view, click through `ensure_schema → extract_bronze → transform_silver → build_gold → data_quality_check` as they go green, open a couple of task logs live | Real orchestration: retries config, task dependencies, actual USGS payload sizes in the logs |
| 18–23 min | `psql -U analytics -d earthquake_analytics -c "SELECT * FROM gold.swarm_signals ORDER BY updated_at DESC LIMIT 10;"` | The actual BI-ready output — this is the "so what" moment |
| 23–27 min | Trigger a second run, show it's still fast/clean (idempotency) | Rerunning doesn't duplicate or break anything |
| 27–30 min | Q&A buffer | — |

If you want a true zero-network fallback in case USGS or your wifi is
uncooperative mid-demo: run `python3 scripts/run_ingestion_standalone.py
--save sample.json` beforehand as a sanity check, and keep the terminal
output from that run as a backup talking point.

